This document gives mathematica code to calculate the Expected Fisher
observation for the three-runner case.  The last bit of the file is R
code to make Fisher_information.pdf, which is a plot of the Expected
Fisher information a function of x.

First, r_true = 1:


p1 = 1/(1 + x + x^2)
p2 = 1/(1 + x) + 1/(1 + x^2) - 2/(1 + x + x^2)
p3 = 1 - 1/(1 + x) - 1/(1 + x^2) + 1/(1 + x + x^2)

t1 = p1*D[Log[p1], {x, 2}] // Together
t2 = p2*D[Log[p2], {x, 2}] // Together
t3 = p3*D[Log[p3], {x, 2}] // Together


Fobs1 = -(t1+t2+t3) // Together




Second, r_true = 2:





p1 = x/(1+x+x^2)
p2 = 1 - 2*x/(1+x+x^2)
p3 = x/(1+x+x^2)

t1 = p1*D[Log[p1], {x, 2}] // Together
t2 = p2*D[Log[p2], {x, 2}] // Together
t3 = p3*D[Log[p3], {x, 2}] // Together


Fobs2 = -(t1+t2+t3) // Together



Third, r_true = 3:

p1 = x^2/(1+x+x^2)
p2 = (x + 2*x^3 + x^4)/((1+x)*(1+x^2)*(1+x+x^2))
p3 = (1+x+2*x^2)/((1+x)*(1+x^2)*(1+x+x^2))

t1 = p1*D[Log[p1], {x, 2}] // Together
t2 = p2*D[Log[p2], {x, 2}] // Together
t3 = p3*D[Log[p3], {x, 2}] // Together


Fobs3 = -(t1+t2+t3) // Together





The above give, in text form:

f1 <- function(x){
(2 + 13*x + 51*x^2 + 102*x^3 + 182*x^4 + 201*x^5 + 195*x^6 + 127*x^7 + 79*x^8 + 34*x^9 + 18*x^10 + 3*x^11 + x^12)/
 (x*(1 + x)*(1 + x^2)^2* (1 + x + x^2)^2*(2 + x + x^2)*(1 + 2*x + x^3))
 }     

f2 <- function(x){
(2*(1 - 2*x^2 + x^4))/(x*(1 - x + x^2)*(1 + x + x^2)^2)
}

f3 <- function(x){
(1 + 3*x + 18*x^2 + 34*x^3 + 79*x^4 + 127*x^5 + 195*x^6 + 201*x^7 + 182*x^8 + 102*x^9 + 51*x^10 + 13*x^11 + 2*x^12)/
 (x*(1 + x)*(1 + x^2)^2*(1 + x + x^2)^2*(1 + x + 2*x^2)*(1 + 2*x^2 + x^3))
}

x <- seq(from=0.1,to=0.9,len=500)

fisherinfo <- function(...){
 plot(x,f2(x),type="n", xlab="x", ylab="Fisher information")
 points(x,f1(x),type="l",col="black")
 points(x,f2(x),type="l",col="red")
 points(x,f3(x),type="l",col="blue")

 legend("topright",
   lty=1, col=c("black","red","blue"),
   legend=c("r=1", "r=2", "r=3")
 )
}

fisherinfo()
pdf(file="Fisher_information.pdf")
fisherinfo()
dev.off()